enly between the two routes. If there are more than two paths, load balancing can be done in various ways (round robin, least connections, etc.).\n\nThis network provides multiple redundant connections for improved reliability and performance. For instance, if one path between Barcelona and Kiev fails, data can still flow through alternative paths like Warsaw-Kiev or Amsterdam-Kiev. Similarly, there are multiple routes from Basel to London (via Rotterdam or directly) which can help improve the overall network's efficiency."}
